          {"id": "c", "text": "Mercury、Mars、Venus、Earth、Pluto、Uranus、Neptune、Saturn、Jupiter。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Order all nine historical masses globally, comparing normalized exponents first and coefficients when exponents agree.",
        "source_solution": "The actual white table gives Mercury 3.17*10^23,Venus 4.87*10^24,Earth 5.98*10^24,Mars 6.40*10^23,Jupiter 1.90*10^27,Saturn 5.69*10^26,Uranus 8.70*10^25,Neptune 1.03*10^26,Pluto 5.40*10^24 kg. Complete increasing order: Mercury,Mars,Venus,Pluto,Earth,Uranus,Neptune,Saturn,Jupiter. The other complete source task has ratio (1.90*10^27)/(5.98*10^24)=95000/299 exactly. This solution was saved in source-solutions-181-SOURCE.json before options.",
        "unit_reason": "One complete nine-body permutation retains the global comparison task and cross-block merging. The ratio is a separate complete task requiring directed division of two values rather than a global order, not a split based merely on printed a/b labels.",
        "concept_blocks": [3],
        "limitations": ["Selecting a complete ordering does not demonstrate independently writing the nine body names in increasing mass order."],
        "figure_observations": [
          {
            "figure_id": "tbl-p0064-01",
            "observation": "Viewed the existing bound white preview at its full 640x320 size exactly once in this recovery pass. Top block: Mercury 3.17*10^23,Venus 4.87*10^24,Earth 5.98*10^24,Mars 6.40*10^23 kg. Bottom block: Jupiter 1.90*10^27,Saturn 5.69*10^26,Uranus 8.70*10^25,Neptune 1.03*10^26,Pluto 5.40*10^24 kg. All names, values, superscripts and rightmost/bottommost borders are readable. The two blocks are a layout division only. Current declared SVG SHA-256 is 18d5481948b31819c9dc95abd53c2ad3230b5566062b9c26005bd7014d2b31e7; the viewed preview SHA-256 is 35aaf83011c3e95dc669dd12883073db269acf8d3c3726b1277df392e0ecac9b. The earlier black view was a theme-resolution preview failure, not missing source data."
          }
        ]
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["b"],
        "rationales": [
          {
            "option_id": "a",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "Ignore every power of ten and sort only the nine coefficients numerically: 1.03 Neptune,1.90 Jupiter,3.17 Mercury,4.87 Venus,5.40 Pluto,5.69 Saturn,5.98 Earth,6.40 Mars,8.70 Uranus. This yields exactly the proposed complete ordering.",
